This is well known.  Radix sort was used to sort cards with the card  
sorters of yesteryear.  The Omega(n log n) lower bound for sorting is  
on the number of comparisons between elements.  Radix sort does not  
treat each element as atomic.  It does not do comparisons between  
whole elements.  It is a kind of bucket sort, and violates the model  
used to prove the lower bound.

